	<Description>Spectrometer containing a blazed (or "echelette") grating, which diffracts the waves from a source that emits 2 wavelengths under 2 slightly different angles. The lens performs a Fourier transform by separating the 2 wavelengths into two spatially separated focal points. You can switch on either source (or rotate the grating) to see the effect of either wavelength.</Description>
